{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggCgnMNpZgyhkUxoCxJ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is in: `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[33, 33, 34]`, so no grosz goes missing. The leftover grosze are spread one each across the last people, so `split_cents(101, 3)` gives `[33, 34, 34]`.\n\nI also had to change `receipt.py`. It was covering for the bug by adding the remainder to the last person's share (`shares[-1] += total % len(people)`). With the fix in place, that line would have charged the remainder twice: a 10 zł bill would have come out as 3,33 / 3,33 / 3,35. I removed it.\n\n**Tests:** I added a test to `test_money.py` and saw it fail before the fix. Because I changed `receipt.py`, I ran `test_receipt.py` as well as `test_money.py`. All 6 tests in the two files pass. As you asked, I didn't run the full suite.\n\nThere's one change in how receipts behave. Before, the last person paid the whole remainder; now it's spread out. For 10,01 zł split three ways, the old version gave 3,33 / 3,33 / 3,35 and the new one gives 3,33 / 3,34 / 3,34.\n\nNothing is committed yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_read_input_tokens":21067,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":795},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c09d29ea-7a98-47c4-9508-49c05a4d3914","uuid":"196336f5-1064-49d3-920f-e061ed9a0681","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:06:22.182Z","request_id":"req_011CggCgn6WLNMHD8u2RV4FM"}
